<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Yen Tu by Motorbike: Choosing a Bike for the Trip</h1>
<p>Choosing a bike for Yen Tu is a corridor problem rather than a mountain problem, because the machine&rsquo;s day is spent on the northeast&rsquo;s long working spine while the climbing belongs to the rider&rsquo;s legs, and the honest choice is the machine that covers distance comfortably, holds its line among commerce and rests quietly while its human walks upward. This guide writes the choice without quoting prices or inventing conditions, because the fleet&rsquo;s current citizens and their honest moods are desk knowledge, refreshed daily at 112 Nguyen Van Cu.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where every machine in the fleet has a file and a biography. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, absorb the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
